Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:23:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] core: add the search operator

search [kind=case_sensitive|case_insensitive] [in (T1, T2*, ...)] Predicate
and the piped form T | search Predicate.

Translated to existing IR: a union (with the $table source column) of one
filter per table, or a filter on the piped input. For each table the
predicate is rewritten into ordinary KQL and bound against that table's
schema:
- a bare string term matches if any string column, or dynamic column via
  tostring(), has it (has / has_cs);
- Col:"term" applies the same test to one column;
- wildcards follow Kusto's mapping, implemented as regexes: "abc*" word
  prefix, "*abc" word suffix, "*abc*" substring, "a*c" \ba.*c\b;
- and / or / parentheses / not() combine terms;
- any other predicate (Col == "x", N > 1) is kept as written and is false
  for a table that lacks one of its columns.
Terms are case-insensitive unless kind=case_sensitive. Without in (...)
every table of the database is searched.

The IRTranslator now receives the query's GlobalState (needed to bind the
rewritten predicate). Limits: the predicate cannot reference let-bound
scalars, in (...) takes database tables only (not let-bound tabular
expressions), and the piped form names rows by the input table only when
the input is a plain table reference (otherwise union_arg0).
